    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterConnectionSectionTitleModern">Website Authorization &amp; Connection</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterConnectionSectionDescriptionLegacy">In legacy compatibility mode, the client uses username and password to call the login endpoint under the Base URL you provide.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterConnectionSectionDescriptionModern">The client never receives or stores your website password. Login opens the browser authorization flow and returns a token.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterBaseUrlDescriptionLegacy">In legacy backend mode, enter the legacy API prefix directly. The client will not rewrite it to /api, but will add a trailing slash if needed.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterBaseUrlDescriptionModern">Website authorization and account queries use this address as their base.</sys:String>
