    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterPageTitle">User Center</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterPageDescription">Website browser authorization is the default. To connect to a legacy backend, enable compatibility mode and fill in the username, password, and the legacy API prefix directly.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterProfileSyncHint">If you changed your username or email on the website, authorize again to sync the latest profile.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterLegacyCompatibilityTitle">Legacy Backend Compatibility</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterLegacyCompatibilityDescription">When enabled, the client uses legacy username/password login and treats Base URL as the legacy API prefix exactly as entered.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterLegacyMigrationGuideTitle">Move legacy users to website sign-in</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterLegacyMigrationGuideDescription">If you still use a legacy account or legacy backend compatibility mode, open the website user center, sign in there, and follow the website prompt to bind your old account. After binding, use website authorization in the client.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterLegacyMigrationGuideStepLogin">1. Click “Bind old account on website” and sign in on the website in your browser.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterLegacyMigrationGuideStepBind">2. In the website user center, follow the prompt to bind the old account, email, or complete verification.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterLegacyMigrationGuideStepReturn">3. Return to the client and click “Switch to website authorization”. Stop using legacy username/password sign-in afterward.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterLegacyMigrationGuideOpenWebsiteButton">Bind old account on website</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="UserCenterLegacyMigrationGuideStartLoginButton">Switch to website authorization</sys:String>
