    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartGuideBadge">Quick Start</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartGuideTitle">Welcome to VRCLS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartGuideSubtitle">VRCLS can recognize and translate microphone audio, desktop audio, or manual text, then send the result through the main window or OSC.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartGuideTip">For the best first run, confirm your input device, recognition language, and target language first. If you want local recognition, open Update Center and download the model.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartListenTitle">Listen Controls</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartListenDescription">The two buttons at the top control microphone and desktop listening. The small level bars help confirm audio is arriving.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartTranscriptTitle">Live Transcript</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartTranscriptDescription">The middle area shows rolling recognition results and multiple translation lines. Click any entry to copy it quickly.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartManualTitle">Manual Send</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartManualDescription">The text box at the bottom is useful for quick typing, sending OSC text, or testing your current translation target.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartSettingsTitle">Settings Center</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartSettingsDescription">Open Settings to switch recognition mode, languages, translation engines, and VRChat / SteamVR integrations.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartGuideRecognitionButton">Recognition Settings</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartGuideUpdateButton">Open Update Center</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartGuideFinishButton">Start Using VRCLS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartGuideTooltip">Open the quick-start guide</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartGuideReopenHint">If you ever forget what something does, click the info button in the top-right corner to open this guide again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartStep1Title">Welcome to VRCLS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartStep1Desc">Let's take a quick tour to get you started with real-time translation for VRChat.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartStep2Title">Listen Controls</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartStep2Desc">The left group controls microphone listening, and the right group controls desktop audio listening. Each slim meter shows the live input level for its own source.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartStep3Title">Live Transcript</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartStep3Desc">Recognition and translation results will scroll here. You can click any transcript line to quickly copy it to clipboard.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartStep4Title">Manual Input</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartStep4Desc">You can also type here to manually translate and send text directly to VRChat without speaking.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartStep5Title">Settings Center</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="QuickStartStep5Desc">Finally, click the gear icon to configure languages, translation engines, local models, and VR integrations. You are all set!</sys:String>
